Attached is a patch for the tmscsim driver, converting it to the new
pci_device interface. Applies to 2.6.3 on the top of the other pending
patches:
my earlier patch, reported on the list and regenerated against 2.6.3:
http://home.arcor.de/g.liakhovetski/scsi/tmscsim-20040304-no_internal_queue.diff
2 patches from Christoph Hellwig:
follow up to my above patch "Re: [PATCH, 2.6] tmscsim - no internal
command-queuing"
http://marc.theaimsgroup.com/?l=linux-scsi&m=107563427310863&w=2
and "[PATCH] remove procfs write support from tmscsim:"
http://marc.theaimsgroup.com/?l=linux-scsi&m=107564997426650&w=2

Works on my machine with the on-board AM53C974 controller. More testing,
in particular in modular build would be nice. Comments welcome as usual.

Kurt, please consider.

Thanks to Christoph for the idea and help
Guennadi
---
Guennadi Liakhovetski




